[{:db/id "q-40218/selection/ae37f5882d4ff79fde6e05e67edf55664eb0956ba007cb0f322d29803171f934" :answer/id #uuid "0a032b3a-9340-518f-ae4f-deb49ac9c02e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40218/selection/16f021b68c2fc8eb76acce17f6c2dfdcf5714890a9c0ce34400c8c64a15788b6" :answer/id #uuid "fca5d6e2-7276-5b98-87b1-643396737379" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40218/selection/b4cd4438f258fdeabd572fa4db999281267adcfe8d7834b1204e54f76bc43f37" :answer/id #uuid "bcc11ec3-bc8f-5041-a2a9-751d2d5c06f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40218/selection/6463127646a2bb374c7293855dd56ea87854b94ee0759e871df0abc01b80d544" :answer/id #uuid "28225b33-f11e-5c79-a815-ac4beb5347fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40218/selection/8a92438bbf11da84fab01847983296a35aef2555efbab7139e635b4740e3883c" :answer/id #uuid "19dc3b36-981e-5f20-9ddb-773f2a8ebda2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40218/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ee1d6a8b-afde-5aab-af3b-1c7dc52cd434" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40218/selection/16f021b68c2fc8eb76acce17f6c2dfdcf5714890a9c0ce34400c8c64a15788b6" :answer-field/choices ["q-40218/selection/ae37f5882d4ff79fde6e05e67edf55664eb0956ba007cb0f322d29803171f934" "q-40218/selection/16f021b68c2fc8eb76acce17f6c2dfdcf5714890a9c0ce34400c8c64a15788b6" "q-40218/selection/b4cd4438f258fdeabd572fa4db999281267adcfe8d7834b1204e54f76bc43f37" "q-40218/selection/6463127646a2bb374c7293855dd56ea87854b94ee0759e871df0abc01b80d544" "q-40218/selection/8a92438bbf11da84fab01847983296a35aef2555efbab7139e635b4740e3883c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40218" :question/id #uuid "0cec22da-e61e-52a7-b865-4b04e5b177ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-40218" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{12\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 0+9\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{12\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 1+9\\cdot (-1)}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40218/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cae73a3-842e-5a1a-8774-35bba342845c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40218"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81475/selection/2c3518c15a2e3706dc7e46408a3cda60c605b99f096663d9f414e6f5852e62c0" :answer/id #uuid "023dd49c-b89a-5f07-b156-948ea5149c7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81475/selection/cb637b83b8ad04c86644b1ab0cd2409959f868480351b800ca29728fc5a033b3" :answer/id #uuid "3ca73bed-4f8a-5dea-946d-4a0a2d53768b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81475/selection/5b22abeeb66df76392c530f61f658189a24a2fc03de025716ba629dc7ce7deae" :answer/id #uuid "4819e040-9ea2-548b-a1dc-692762ca08aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81475/selection/b74a2fcdfac401d07e2dfc5a434f12064f8d6a063caccf3a26297531a9690e4b" :answer/id #uuid "e880bf85-7ffc-5d31-b65b-0647f46f4385" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81475/selection/ce975ad161c6280e907d107982634ca642bec601ba97000ade33879c5be99a48" :answer/id #uuid "3dcbf7ee-4a6c-5a77-aac8-d635f5f58be9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81475/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d193bf6-73c8-5f43-8426-77b23487de91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81475/selection/2c3518c15a2e3706dc7e46408a3cda60c605b99f096663d9f414e6f5852e62c0" :answer-field/choices ["q-81475/selection/2c3518c15a2e3706dc7e46408a3cda60c605b99f096663d9f414e6f5852e62c0" "q-81475/selection/cb637b83b8ad04c86644b1ab0cd2409959f868480351b800ca29728fc5a033b3" "q-81475/selection/5b22abeeb66df76392c530f61f658189a24a2fc03de025716ba629dc7ce7deae" "q-81475/selection/b74a2fcdfac401d07e2dfc5a434f12064f8d6a063caccf3a26297531a9690e4b" "q-81475/selection/ce975ad161c6280e907d107982634ca642bec601ba97000ade33879c5be99a48"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81475" :question/id #uuid "6ea59652-3e77-5eac-9804-089948d56101" :question/math-academy-id "q-81475" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}},$ $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}},$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{3}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{4\\cdot 1+6\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 0+(-17)\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}{a}_{1}=-\\frac{24}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{4\\cdot 3+6\\cdot (-5)+3\\cdot 0+(-17)\\cdot 1}{{3}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=-\\frac{35}{35}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{3}}{{a}_{3}\\cdot {a}_{3}}{a}_{3}=\\frac{4\\cdot 11+6\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 0+(-17)\\cdot (-8)}{{11}^{2}+{5}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-8)^{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{210}{210}[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81475/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cae73a3-842e-5a1a-8774-35bba342845c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81475"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81583/selection/b3ea024b22165e01dfb8c4e4abfe9971f1a724d29578729aaf2203a15e64151f" :answer/id #uuid "70af7eda-dcbb-57a6-968c-9675d9b992b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81583/selection/b70f14b1c5f8bd844f272604b4678054f03793a3a6c66f52d98653d95ad2fec7" :answer/id #uuid "2b46d486-f3fb-53fb-8547-baa0f547b3e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81583/selection/56e367cc7a53b7c4974adebc3f4bf0a582270c83e11e27b1428f5f56392b15eb" :answer/id #uuid "679c0874-e0e8-5b5f-8ef5-a9a5352b62c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81583/selection/166877bd2b5a5fc4f9a18a1b8dd48bc83cf34ab1c01727c9a38a1d43361ce79a" :answer/id #uuid "e9bfcf0a-51af-5545-a02e-f1dc720ea602" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81583/selection/9d898666dd44b89330e338dd014f3fccbfc102872544fda023df30b4b5f9cf7c" :answer/id #uuid "ba8f30fc-06e0-5b94-a10d-9c2eefe60951" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81583/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a987de74-ab99-510b-8448-aed7cc6d57ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81583/selection/9d898666dd44b89330e338dd014f3fccbfc102872544fda023df30b4b5f9cf7c" :answer-field/choices ["q-81583/selection/b3ea024b22165e01dfb8c4e4abfe9971f1a724d29578729aaf2203a15e64151f" "q-81583/selection/b70f14b1c5f8bd844f272604b4678054f03793a3a6c66f52d98653d95ad2fec7" "q-81583/selection/56e367cc7a53b7c4974adebc3f4bf0a582270c83e11e27b1428f5f56392b15eb" "q-81583/selection/166877bd2b5a5fc4f9a18a1b8dd48bc83cf34ab1c01727c9a38a1d43361ce79a" "q-81583/selection/9d898666dd44b89330e338dd014f3fccbfc102872544fda023df30b4b5f9cf7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81583" :question/id #uuid "079d68d2-f09f-5313-8733-bae2b03b6897" :question/math-academy-id "q-81583" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the plane given that $v⊥w.$" :question/worked-solution "Since our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ \nAnd, since the set ${v,w}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{(-2)\\cdot (-3)+(-2)\\cdot 2+(-9)\\cdot 1}{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}v=-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 2+(-9)\\cdot (-1)}{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}w=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81583/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acb4bd03-9b89-5775-a700-e1f3ea9fa62e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81583"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81580/selection/48f3c0928769041137602624fa45a618f0d90f13990b72fae6f17108d6fba94a" :answer/id #uuid "3ec8b575-341a-56ed-a333-efc9606a2181" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81580/selection/c121d845cac988ff01796010ec2e8184de653fe3cf4c421172cffc1016b56efb" :answer/id #uuid "c194a635-49bd-5063-ad3d-2ce922af9175" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81580/selection/273c8365c3c81f363972bb400cf4be0b495e1dc6db74dabfa80ae6f4b4230765" :answer/id #uuid "7b3050ac-8837-5759-9d63-26f73afc4fcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81580/